.TH omf_record_begin 3
.SH NAME
omf_record_begin \- get pointer to start of record data
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include "omf.h"

void* \fBomf_record_begin\fP(omf_record* \fIrec\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBomf_record_begin\fP returns a pointer to the start of the data payload within an OMF record \fIrec\fR.

It parses specific record types (such as PUBDEF) to skip header fields (e.g. group index, segment index, base frame) and return a pointer to the first nested structure or data element. Returns NULL if the record type is not supported for automatic parsing.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
omf_record_end(3), omf_record_next(3)